// =============================================================================
// Chora Content Consumption — KnowledgeGraph events
// =============================================================================
//
// Aggregate roots:
//   - KnowledgeGraphNode + KnowledgeGraphEdge (legacy Discovery topology)
//   - MapCluster + Exploration + HexagonNode + TrailHop
//     (per-user hexagonal exploration fog per ADR-143)
// Owning domain  : Content Consumption (chora_consumption DB).
// Topic prefix   : chora.consumption.{aggregate}.*
//
// Discovery mode (per skill SKILL.md) uses PostgreSQL Recursive CTEs over
// kg_node + kg_edge in chora_consumption — NOT a separate graph DB.
// Edges are typed: prerequisite_of, extends, analogy_of, contrasts_with,
// applied_in. Per-tenant RLS enforced on every recursive frame.
//
// Per ADR-143, knowledge_graph_edges (originally in chora_creation) is
// relocated to chora_consumption and renamed atom_semantic_edges. The
// new per-user feature adds 9 event topics covering MapCluster lifecycle,
// Exploration lifecycle, HexagonFog cache, and JunctionDetected (when fog
// generation finds an overlap with another of the user's active clusters).
//
// These events surface curiosity signals to Sharing (reputation, leaderboards)
// and Observability (engagement analytics), and feed the AI Kernel cost
// ledger via HexagonFogGenerated.total_cost_micros.
// =============================================================================

